From: C2000-MAX firmware build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: mediatek: reset retained MT7987 state before firmware

The internal MT7987 2.5G PHY loader marks the XBZ, PMA and RX blocks as
DO_NOT_RESET while loading DSP data.  Those bits can survive a warm SoC
reset, so the BMCR reset at the next boot does not necessarily return the
PHY to the same state as a power-on reset.  Clear the retention mask before
the existing reset and firmware reload sequence.

This is deliberately done at probe rather than only in a reboot notifier so
watchdog and crash resets follow the same recovery path.

--- a/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-2p5ge.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-2p5ge.c
@@ -412,6 +412,11 @@ static int mt7987_2p5ge_phy_load_fw(stru
 
 	phy_lock_mdio_bus(phydev);
 
+	/* A warm SoC reset may retain the internal PHY analog/DSP state. */
+	reg_clear_bits(priv, MTK_2P5GPHY_PMD_REG + DO_NOT_RESET,
+		       DO_NOT_RESET_XBZ | DO_NOT_RESET_PMA | DO_NOT_RESET_RX);
+	usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+
 	/* Force 2.5Gphy back to AN state */
 	__phy_set_bits(phydev, MII_BMCR, BMCR_RESET);
 	usleep_range(5000, 6000);
